{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And their dominion perished, from Heshbon to Dibon.</b> The city of Heshbon — its dominion perished over all the land as far as Dibon, so that no ruler of Moab would ever again rule over it." "<b>ניר.</b> In the sense of dominion/ruler, as in 'that my servant David may have ניר' (II Sam 3:21). Another interpretation: <b>ונירם</b> — in the sense of casting, as in 'ירה into the sea' (Exod 15:4); the meaning is: we cast them from their land. And if you wish to interpret it as the Targum does, it should have been pointed ונירם with a vowel on the vav. Another interpretation: <b>ונירם</b> — in the sense of ניר and plowing, as in 'נירו לכם ניר' (Jer 4:3), which indicates concerning it (the land)." "<b>ונשים.</b> In the sense of desolation — that is to say: we plowed and made desolate their cities." "<b>ונירם.</b> It is pointed with a יבדילנו-type accent (disjunctive), to exclude — our masculine form; and so many others." "<b>ונשים עד נפח אשר עד מידבא.</b> It is punctuated (with special pointing) upon it, to teach that even beyond that, the same was the case."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:10.555544894Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}